  "math_review": {
    "centered_increment_formula": "rho*cp*fsum(V_HEX/8*fsum(T_end_node-T_begin_node)) over all active regular HEX8 cells",
    "reason": "The integral of each trilinear shape function on an axis-aligned HEX8 cell is V/8. For constant rho and cp, summing nodal differences is the exact integral form and avoids subtracting large independent enthalpy inventories. math.fsum stabilizes cell/cumulative sums; it does not create exact native temperatures.",
    "nonconstant_cp_refused_and_fixed_card_scalars_bound": true,
    "birth_handling": "At activation, begin already contains new350K nodes and preserved shared/existing values; comparing end to that same begin excludes birth inventory from accumulated PDE heat. The unchanged declared birth field keeps shared interface values, not a uniform350K assumption.",
    "initial_and_birth_enthalpy_are_bookkeeping_only": "e0 and birth_energy retain donor integrations; enthalpy_J is reconstructed e0+birth_energy+cumulative_centered_heat. None is subtracted to decide step or continuous acceptance.",
    "step_gate": "delta_h-dt*quadrature_power+zero_constant_cp_capacity_correction, unchanged absolute1e-7J",
    "continuous_gate": "fsum(centered increments)-integrated finite-box source, divided by max(abs(source energy),1e-12); unchanged numeric1% threshold now measures source response and is stricter than inventory normalization.",
    "source_off_detection": "A positive q_seen material may survive removing its PDE kernel; source-value checks alone are insufficient. With zero delta_h, the actual centered step expression remains -dt*qh and source-normalized cumulative defect is -1 when positive source input is omitted.",
    "source_scale_only_not_solution": "Full-space normalization is40W and at most16J over0.4s; rho*cp=2.43e6J/(m3*K), so old1m3/400K/reference300K inventory is2.43e8J. These analytical scale statements are not a solved field.",
    "numeric_limits": "Stored native temperature quantization, solve/CSV errors, endpoint source quadrature and time-discretization error may still cause refusal. CSV17 preserves binary64 roundtrip; no passing result or exact epigraph/physical equivalence is assumed. No tolerance relaxation or fitted post-run gate."
  },
